# Code owners for the trust boundary. With "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled on the main branch protection rule, a PR touching any path below
# cannot merge until one of its owners approves. Keep at least two owners per
# line: an author's own approval never counts, so a single-owner path would
# deadlock on that owner's own PRs.
#
# The paths mirror verify/check_submission_scope.py's critical set: everything
# that defines what the board accepts. Last matching line wins.

# CI definitions: on pull_request events GitHub runs the PR's own copy of the
# workflow, so the only real defense on workflow edits is merge-time review.
/.github/                       @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela

# The verifier stack, the schema, and the site builder that renders verdicts.
/verify/                        @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/decode/                        @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/schema/                        @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/site/build.py                  @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela

# Dependency and build inputs the verifier runs under.
/Makefile                       @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/pyproject.toml                 @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/uv.lock                        @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela
/run_tests.py                   @FarLab @vprusso @MathysRennela

# The pinned hashes of the trusted validation stack. A re-pin is the loud,
# reviewable signal that verifier semantics changed; owner review is what
